course: dictionary
lesson: 6096
title: Metric
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Metric is a word about measuring. A system is metric when it is based on the metre, the kilogram and the litre, and its units go up in tens. «France created the metric system in the 1790s, and most of the world now uses it.» So the metric system is one set of measures that all link together.
explain: The clue is in the units. Ten millimetres make one centimetre, 100 centimetres make one metre, and 1,000 metres make one kilometre. To change from one unit to another, you multiply or divide by 10, 100 or 1,000.
explain: «Kings and cities set standard weights and measures so buyers were not cheated.» Standard means everyone uses the same measure, so nobody can trick you. The metric system is one of these standard systems, and it is used in most of the world.
explain: Metric can also be a noun, meaning a measure used to judge how well something is doing, such as test scores or sales. In maths and science lessons, metric almost always means measuring with metric units. Imperial units such as inches, feet, pounds and pints are used partly in the UK and still widely in the USA.
fact: Metric means using the metre, the kilogram and the litre as the main units of measurement.
fact: Metric units go up in tens: 10, 100, 1,000.
fact: «France created the metric system in the 1790s, and most of the world now uses it.»
fact: Metric system, metric units and metric ton are common phrases in maths and science.
fact: Inches, feet, pounds and pints are imperial units, not metric units.
exercise: «France created the metric system in the 1790s.» What is the metric system? | A list of the best test scores | A kind of poem with a set rhythm | A system of counting in twelves | *A way of measuring based on the metre, the kilogram and the litre
exercise: How many centimetres make one metre? | 10 | 12 | 1,000 | *100
exercise: Which of these is a metric unit of length? | Pint | Yard | *Metre | Inch
test: If you have 1,000 metres, how many kilometres is that? | *1 | 10 | 1,000 | 100
test: Which of these is an imperial unit? | Gram | Kilogram | Litre | *Pound
exam: Which pair of units is metric? | *Metres and litres | Feet and pints | Yards and gallons | Inches and pounds
